<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sweden</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Swedish</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sweden is a kingdom in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> on the eastern side of the Scandinavian Peninsula. In the seventeenth century it became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swedish-empire">Swedish Empire</a>, a Baltic great power whose armies intervened decisively in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War and fought repeatedly against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>. Its defeat by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a>'s Russia in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-northern-war">Great Northern War</a> ended its imperial era and helped launch the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sweden.jpg" alt="Sweden" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jon Harald Søby and others. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Sweden.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
